n blocks remaining in the 2x3 grid (center was clicked)\nTotal: 8 green blocks remaining\nLet me click all of them to complete the level. I need to find their positions.", "kind": "reasoning", "inContext": false}, {"label": "TOOL CALL: python", "content": "<tool_call>\n<function=python>\n<parameter=code>\n# Check current green blocks and click them all\nseg = current_frame.segmentation\ngreen = [n for n in seg['nodes'] if n['color'] == 'N']\nprint(f\"Green blocks: {len(green)}\")\n\n# Calculate center of each green block for clicking\nclicks = []\nfor g in green:\n    # Get approximate center from boundary\n    rows = [p[0] for p in g['boundary']]\n    cols = [p[1] for p in g['boundary']]\n    center_row = sum(rows) // len(rows)\n    center_col = sum(cols) // len(cols)\n    clicks.append({'action': 'MOUSE', 'row': center_row, 'col': center_col})\n    print(f\"  Click at row={center_row}, col={center_col}\")\n\n# Execute all clicks\naction(clicks)\n</parameter>\n</function>\n</tool_call>", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}, {"label": "TOOL RESULT: python", "content": "Green blocks: 8\n  Click at row=15, col=27\n  Click at row=15, col=33\n  Click at row=15, col=39\n  Click at row=33, col=15\n  Click at row=33, col=27\n  Click at row=39, col=15\n  Click at row=39, col=21\n  Click at row=39, col=27", "kind": "tool", "inContext": true}], "hasExactModelContext": false, "requestIndexWithinTurn": null, "messageCount": 0}}}